6 "Section 2.
7
8 (a) There is appropriated five hundred fifty thousand
9 dollars ($550,000.00) from the general fund to the University of
10 Wyoming to provide medical education and training, and
11 administrative costs thereof, for the first cohort of five (5)
12 students under an agreement with the University of Utah school of
13 medicine. Funds from this general fund appropriation shall be
14 expended by the University of Wyoming provided that:
15
16 (i) The board of trustees of the University of Wyoming
17 has entered into a contract with the University of Utah school of
18 medicine under W.S. 21-17-109;
19
20 (ii) Students receiving medical education and training
21 under this section shall comply with the state of Utah's diversity,
22 equity and inclusion laws as they pertain to instruction and
23 training provided at the University of Utah school of medicine;
24
25 (iii) The board of trustees of the University of
26 Wyoming obtains an agreement with any student receiving medical
27 education and training as specified in W.S. 21-17-109(d); and
28
29 (iv) All other provisions of W.S. 21-17-109 are
30 satisfied.
31
32 (b) This appropriation shall not be transferred or expended
33 for any other purpose. It is the intent of the legislature that
34 this appropriation be doubled and funding for five (5) additional
35 medical students each academic year be included in the University
36 of Wyoming's standard budget for the immediately succeeding fiscal
37 biennium.".
